WEBVTT

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:26.560
Speaker 1: You see, something I learned as someone who tries to go to the gym as regularly as I can, is the principle of hypertrophy.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.620
Speaker 1: And you're going to see how this applies to prayer.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.260
Speaker 1: Because, you see, there are a lot of people who go to the gym regularly but don't see the results.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.140
Speaker 1: And they are wondering why they don't see the result.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:43.940
Speaker 1: And I was in that shoe before until someone explained something to me, my gym instructor, actually.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:52.540
Speaker 1: The concept of hypertrophy is this, that for your muscle to grow bigger, you must stress the muscle enough in.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:01:00.450
Speaker 1: In exercise for some cells, or are they called tissues, to die and grow again bigger.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:13.650
Speaker 1: But the problem is, even if you are doing a lot of work, if you don't work out until failure, until you feel like you have really exhausted yourself, you are not really going to get the results.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.850
Speaker 1: So some people walk out, but they don't work out enough.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:21.200
Speaker 1: There is such a thing as not working out enough.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.920
Speaker 1: There is such a thing as not exercising enough.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:34.640
Speaker 1: There's a graph for it, you know, so there is a level where the workout actually now begins to work, you know, where the muscle is actually being built.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.720
Speaker 1: And it is that point where you're almost to the point of failure.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:47.360
Speaker 1: And then the tissues, forgive me, I'm not a scientist, either tissues or muscles themselves begin to.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.110
Speaker 1: To break a little bit so that they can grow again bigger.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.030
Speaker 1: It is at that point that you can say hypertrophy has happened.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:02:02.310
Speaker 1: Well, the Bible is no stranger to allusions and metaphors.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:14.390
Speaker 1: So when Paul, for instance, says bodily exercise profits little, he's telling you metaphorically that there is what to learn about exercise vis a vis our spiritual exercise.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.030
Speaker 1: There's such a thing as spiritual exercise.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:25.880
Speaker 1: And I believe that, amongst many things, hypertrophy is one of the things that we can learn that indeed there is such a thing as not praying enough.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.600
Speaker 1: There is such a thing as not praying enough.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:36.200
Speaker 1: You see, when Jesus went to Peter, I think I said this yesterday or day before at Gethsemane to find him sleeping.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.760
Speaker 1: He said, what could you not watch with me one hour?

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.080
Speaker 1: And I mean, that means.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.040
Speaker 1: Listen to me.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.190
Speaker 1: It doesn't mean that Peter didn't pray.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.150
Speaker 1: Peter did not pray enough.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:54.190
Speaker 1: There is such a thing as not praying enough, especially in some certain instances.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.870
Speaker 1: If I have enough time, I'll touch on how to know when it's enough.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.270
Speaker 1: All right?

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.150
Speaker 1: It's a spiritual thing.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:01.070
Speaker 1: It's not about how much you sweat.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:04.190
Speaker 1: This is a way it differs from bodily exercise.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:04.990
Speaker 1: Okay?

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:12.650
Speaker 1: But I'm just here to tell you that Two things are important in prayer, in case you never knew this, volume and consistency.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:13.690
Speaker 1: Never forget this.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.650
Speaker 1: When it comes to prayer, two things are very important.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.050
Speaker 1: Volume and consistency.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.530
Speaker 1: So you need to make sure that you're praying enough and consistently.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.850
Speaker 1: So, you see, a lot of us make this mistake also.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:32.570
Speaker 1: We go to the gym in some really nice gym outfits.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.810
Speaker 1: Really, really nice gym outfits.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:43.430
Speaker 1: And then we go there, we take a few pictures, we just lift some things around and then we don't show up.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.190
Speaker 1: We go into oblivion for the next one year.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:51.670
Speaker 1: And then maybe after we have a new year resolution, we show up again.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.870
Speaker 1: That is what we do.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:57.870
Speaker 1: And I'm sure I don't have to tell you that you can't gain results that way.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.430
Speaker 1: You can't gain results that way.

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:03.270
Speaker 1: So not only is volume important, consistency is important.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:04.620
Speaker 1: All right.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:10.780
Speaker 1: So some people go to the gym and the lifts they are carrying are just too light.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:11.740
Speaker 1: Too light.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:13.420
Speaker 1: They can't do the work.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.020
Speaker 1: Too light.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.180
Speaker 1: There's another extreme.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.980
Speaker 1: Some people, the lift is too heavy, so they can't keep a proper form.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.700
Speaker 1: But for many people, it's too light.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:32.100
Speaker 1: Because you see, when you have the light with the proper weight, another thing you must get right is the volume.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:39.220
Speaker 1: You must continue to, for instance, if it's a bicep curl, move your arm often enough for the work to begin to work.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.980
Speaker 1: And that's why the first few reps, you don't feel anything.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.940
Speaker 1: It is as time goes on that you begin to feel the impact.

00:04:46.579 --> 00:04:48.020
Speaker 1: Isn't that how it works?

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:52.180
Speaker 1: So understand this prayer works like a battery.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:53.940
Speaker 1: Never forget this.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.460
Speaker 1: It works like a battery.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.180
Speaker 1: And that is spiritual energy.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.000
Speaker 1: I'll give you two texts that emphasize this.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:06.000
Speaker 1: It says, the effectual, fervent prayer of a right makes tremendous power available.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:09.040
Speaker 1: Think about that.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.800
Speaker 1: That's battery right there.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:13.760
Speaker 1: Battery power.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.040
Speaker 1: It makes tremendous power available.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.560
Speaker 1: James 5:16b.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.320
Speaker 1: It tells you that prayer has a cumulative effect, a build up.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:36.140
Speaker 1: I'm telling you, more often than not someone who has been in the Lord 10 years, 15 years, you cannot compare the spiritual investment of that person to someone who has been in Lord 5 years.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.340
Speaker 1: In case you have not heard it before, hear it now.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:52.670
Speaker 1: Except if the person who has been in the Lord for shorter, maybe has a better teacher, quicker understanding, and is able to exercise himself more.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:06:00.270
Speaker 1: But usually that time will count because spiritual exercises have a cumulative effect.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.230
Speaker 1: Cumulative effect.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:11.870
Speaker 1: And this is why, when Lazarus is sick and dies, Jesus stayed praying for four days.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:16.110
Speaker 1: And he can come and say, father, I thank you that you have heard me already.

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:17.800
Speaker 1: You have Heard me already.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.480
Speaker 1: And he now points.

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:20.600
Speaker 1: Or he didn't point.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.880
Speaker 1: He just says with a loud voice, lazarus, come forth.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.440
Speaker 1: That's cumulative power at work there.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:34.200
Speaker 1: He had charged himself to the degree all he needed to do was to give the command.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:35.800
Speaker 1: Another text.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:45.850
Speaker 1: But, you, beloved, building up yourself on your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Ghost, brick upon brick.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:07:00.210
Speaker 1: You know, I've told you the Greek word, there is a deregative derivative of the Greek word oikodomio, which means it's a building term, a building construction term to lay brick upon brick.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.170
Speaker 1: Brick upon brick.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.290
Speaker 1: Just imagine, some of you have experienced this.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.610
Speaker 1: There's a building construction somewhere on your street.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:17.020
Speaker 1: And then maybe you travel for two weeks and you discover they've made progress, or you are not paying attention, you're passing another route out of the house.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:21.340
Speaker 1: And then the next time you're passing, they're at roof level the next time you're passing.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:35.690
Speaker 1: So he's telling you can do that to your spirit, that by spiritual investment, there can be a new coach in your spirit, a new layer, a new level, just by spiritual investment.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:37.450
Speaker 1: All right?

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.930
Speaker 1: And that's all I want to tell you today.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:44.410
Speaker 1: And so to practice hypertrophy, two things you must do.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.690
Speaker 1: You must pray every day.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.250
Speaker 1: You must pray every day.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.650
Speaker 1: You must pray every day.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:54.890
Speaker 1: Because the volume is important.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.170
Speaker 1: I beg your pardon?

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.250
Speaker 1: The consistency is important.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:00.100
Speaker 1: Pray every day.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:03.860
Speaker 1: Just learn to show up every day.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.380
Speaker 1: It may help to have a prayer time.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:10.500
Speaker 1: All right, Pray every day.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:26.660
Speaker 1: I have gone so far as to say that I believe that someone who has a consistent, albeit shorter, prayer time will have more spiritual results than someone who prays much longer once in a while.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.520
Speaker 1: I believe that with all my heart.

00:08:32.039 --> 00:08:36.400
Speaker 1: It's good that you can spend maybe seven hours stretch praying.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:37.000
Speaker 1: That's good.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:42.600
Speaker 1: But I believe that someone who does 45 minutes every day.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.640
Speaker 1: In fact, let me make it more controversial.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:56.930
Speaker 1: Someone who does 20 minutes every day will eventually have a more healthy work with God than someone who does seven hours once a month.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.770
Speaker 1: That is my opinion.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:05.970
Speaker 1: But I have discovered when it comes to spiritual exercise that consistency is key.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:11.650
Speaker 1: I've taught on long praying, so this is not an excuse for you to reduce how long you pray.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:17.090
Speaker 1: Number two, pray until you warm your heart.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:17.970
Speaker 1: Every day.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:19.950
Speaker 1: Pray until you warm your heart.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:25.630
Speaker 1: You don't want Jesus, who is the same yesterday, today, forever, by the way, saying, oh, could you not watch one hour?

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:27.950
Speaker 1: Could you not watch 45 minutes?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.070
Speaker 1: So it means that there are.

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:36.910
Speaker 1: There is a kind of spiritual work that must be done that requires a Certain amount of time.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.190
Speaker 1: Now, some people do this in the flesh.

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:43.230
Speaker 1: If you are not careful, you allow the devil torment you with this.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.790
Speaker 1: You can pray even three days stretch.

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:50.980
Speaker 1: And then when you're done, you know, you start feeling guilty, like you've not prayed enough.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:53.220
Speaker 1: The devil torments people like that.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:55.540
Speaker 1: If you're not careful, prayer will never be enough.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:57.140
Speaker 1: It will never be enough.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:05.500
Speaker 1: And the devil will just drive you into, you know, almost depression, thinking it's never enough.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.740
Speaker 1: That's another extreme.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.180
Speaker 1: That's a lie of the devil.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:15.160
Speaker 1: Okay, but when?

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.320
Speaker 1: So how do you know from your spirit?

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.240
Speaker 1: A note of victory?

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:19.880
Speaker 1: You just know.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:21.560
Speaker 1: You just know.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:23.400
Speaker 1: You just know.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.440
Speaker 1: Have you ever prayed and you knew it is done?

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:27.880
Speaker 1: It's done.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.720
Speaker 1: You are sure it's done.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:31.400
Speaker 1: That's what I'm talking about.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:39.000
Speaker 1: You know something else, just like Jesus, if you feel it is not done, you can come back to it.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.140
Speaker 1: Jesus divided his prayer into three.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.580
Speaker 1: At the Garden of Gethsemane, he prayed three times.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:53.180
Speaker 1: And if Jesus could pray three times on a night as special as that, it tells you can too.

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:55.020
Speaker 1: You can adjourn.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.460
Speaker 1: Even if you feel like you are not done.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.860
Speaker 1: It doesn't mean you have to pray it through in one stretch.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:05.540
Speaker 1: Except if the Lord categorically tells you that you can take a break and come back.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:06.540
Speaker 1: And that's another thing.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:10.430
Speaker 1: You can take a break and come back.

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:11.510
Speaker 1: You can take pauses.

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:14.630
Speaker 1: Let me tell you, and never forget this.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.230
Speaker 1: There are some things you give 21 days.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:21.590
Speaker 1: Aye, my God.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:33.510
Speaker 1: If you learn this, if you learn to give a matter 21 days, 7 days, 30 days, every day for 20 minutes, just 20 minutes.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:38.650
Speaker 1: The Bible says Jesus came and repeated the same words.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:46.650
Speaker 1: The power of spiritual investment just repeating the same words.

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:49.130
Speaker 1: I cannot overemphasize how important it is.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:58.010
Speaker 1: See, when the devil learns that you know how to stick To a matter 21 days, he will play with you less.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:03.700
Speaker 1: He will only come your way if he's sure you are ready.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.580
Speaker 1: This girl, she's crazy.

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.300
Speaker 1: She can give 90 days on a matter.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:11.700
Speaker 1: All right, all right.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.900
Speaker 1: Hypertrophy is going to change your life.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:19.340
Speaker 1: If you have learned anything in this discipleship, stick to hypertrophy.

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:39.810
Speaker 1: And I believe it's going to change your life, Sam.
